WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.792
Email standardization starts with a small set of explainable transformations.

00:00:04.792 --> 00:00:10.877
Trim boundary spaces. Convert empty strings to NULL if blank means missing.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:15.382
Lowercase the value for a consistent analytical representation.

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:17.827
This does not validate the email.

00:00:17.827 --> 00:00:21.737
It only standardizes the representation before validation.

00:00:21.737 --> 00:00:27.472
Standardization should make equivalent values comparable without inventing facts.

00:00:27.472 --> 00:00:35.712
Lowercasing an email or normalizing a known category map is different from guessing what an ambiguous value

00:00:35.712 --> 00:00:40.948
was supposed to mean. Good cleaning reduces representation noise while preserving uncertainty.
